course: dictionary
lesson: 13919
title: Leadership
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Leadership is a noun, and it has three main meanings. It can mean being the leader of a group, team or country. It can mean the ability to lead people well, which is to guide them, make decisions and help everyone work together. It can also mean the group of people who lead an organisation or party.
explain: «Our class captain showed good leadership by helping everyone find their seat.» Here leadership means the ability to lead well. The captain guided the class and helped others, so the word describes what she did.
explain: «The leadership of the school council meets every Monday.» Here leadership means the group of people who lead. The clue is meets: a group meets, but a single skill does not.
explain: Look at the words around leadership to find its meaning. Words like captain, team, guide and decide are clues. Then swap your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
fact: Leadership means being a leader, or the ability to lead people well.
fact: Leadership can also mean the group of people who lead an organisation, team or party.
fact: Leadership skills include guiding others, making fair decisions and helping people work together.
fact: «The captain shows leadership on the pitch» means the captain guides and encourages the team.
fact: Leadership is an uncountable noun, so we say good leadership, not a good leaderships.
exercise: «Our team captain showed great leadership during the match.» What does leadership mean here? | Running the fastest lap | Being the tallest player on the pitch | Scoring the most goals in the match | *Being good at guiding and helping the team
exercise: «The leadership of the school council met to plan the trip.» What does leadership mean in this sentence? | The room where the school council meets | A kind of school trip | *The people who lead the school council | The rules of the playground
exercise: «Ella was chosen as class captain because she had good leadership skills.» What are leadership skills? | Fast running on the playground | Writing very neatly | *The ability to guide and help others work together | Skill at drawing pictures
test: «The town grew quickly under the leadership of its new mayor.» What does leadership suggest here? | *The guidance and decisions of the mayor who led the town | A type of town map | The mayor's favourite food | A long walk through the town centre
test: Jayden says leadership is just a fancy word for captain. Why is that not quite right? | Leadership means losing a game | Leadership is an animal | *Leadership is a word for a group of people who lead, not a person who wears a badge | Leadership can mean the ability to lead well, not just a job title
exam: «The new head teacher showed strong leadership when the school flooded.» Which word best matches leadership? | Sleeping late | Confusion | Swimming | *Guiding and organising people well in a hard time
